Description:
## PTR-AI-006 — Dynamic pricing intelligence (venue & rental)

**Goal:** Give venue owners and rental brokers an AI pricing assistant that analyzes comparable listings, occupancy, and demand signals to suggest optimal price adjustments. Surfaces as a `CopilotSidebar` chat response and a standalone widget on the pricing settings page.

---

## Scope

Partner types covered: Venue Owner, Real Estate Broker (rental). Not applicable to: restaurants, cafés, event hosts (they have fixed ticket pricing).

Activated via capability flag `partnerAgent.capabilities.revenue` — only shown when flag is true.

---

## `suggest_price_adjustment` tool

```ts
suggest_price_adjustment({
  partner_id: string,
  listing_id: string,       // venue or rental
  listing_type: "venue" | "rental",
  time_window_days?: number, // default 30
})
// Returns:
// {
//   current_price: number,
//   suggested_price: number,
//   direction: "increase" | "decrease" | "hold",
//   confidence: "high" | "medium" | "low",
//   rationale: string,           // Gemini-generated 1-2 sentences
//   comparable_count: number,
//   occupancy_rate: number,
// }
```

### Comparable analysis (Supabase queries)

* Venues: `venue_bookings` — occupancy rate for same neighborhood + capacity range in last 30d
* Rentals: `rentals` + `rental_inquiries` — inquiry-to-booking conversion for comparable sqft/neighborhood
* Places API pgvector: semantic similarity to find "comparable" listings by description embedding

### Gemini rationale generation

System prompt includes: comparable price range, occupancy rate, seasonal factors (if peak period detected from event calendar), partner's current revenue trend.

---

## HITL price update

When partner asks "update my price" from the suggestion:

```tsx
useCopilotAction({
  name: "suggest_price_adjustment",
  available: "disabled",
  render: ({ result, respond }) => (
    <PricingInsightCard
      current={result.current_price}
      suggested={result.suggested_price}
      direction={result.direction}
      rationale={result.rationale}
      occupancyRate={result.occupancy_rate}
      onApply={() => respond({ action: "apply", price: result.suggested_price })}
      onCustom={(p) => respond({ action: "apply", price: p })}
      onDismiss={() => respond({ action: "dismiss" })}
    />
  ),
});
```

`respond({ action: "apply" })` triggers a Supabase update to `partner_locations.price_per_hour` (venue) or `rentals.price_monthly` (rental). **Price-lock rule**: never mutates a price if there are confirmed bookings/tickets at the old price — tool must check first.

---

## Pricing settings page widget

On `/partner/settings/pricing`:

* `PricingInsightCard` always visible (not just in sidebar)
* "Refresh" button re-runs `suggest_price_adjustment`
* Shows last 3 price change history from `revenue_ledger`

---

## Supabase

No new tables. Reads `venue_bookings`, `partner_locations`, `rentals`, `revenue_ledger`. Writes to `partner_locations.price_per_hour` or `rentals.price_monthly` after HITL approval.

Price-lock guard: `SELECT COUNT(*) FROM venue_bookings WHERE venue_id = $1 AND status = 'confirmed' AND price_locked_at > NOW() - INTERVAL '30 days'` — if > 0, block the update and surface a warning.

---

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] `suggest_price_adjustment` returns suggestion with direction + confidence + rationale
- [ ] Only activates for venue/rental partner types (capability flag check)
- [ ] HITL card renders in sidebar and on pricing settings page
- [ ] Price-lock guard blocks update when confirmed bookings exist at old price
- [ ] "Apply" sends HITL response → Supabase update fires
- [ ] Gemini rationale is ≤ 2 sentences, grounded in comparable data
- [ ] Vitest: price-lock guard, suggestion direction logic
- [ ] Playwright: venue partner → pricing page → suggestion card visible → approve flow

---

## Blocked by

* SAN-803 (PTR-AI-004) — pricing tool exposed via AI Workspace
* SAN-705 (AGT-PTR-01) — capability flags must be wired (revenue flag)

## Related

* AGT-PTR-09 (SAN TBD) — revenue insights tool (reads same revenue_ledger)

## CRM-011 — Mastra CRM tools foundation (data-access layer for Phase 2 AI)

**Goal:** Create the 5 core Mastra tools that Phase 2 AI agents will build on. These are pure data-access tools — they query Supabase and return structured results. No Gemini calls, no generative output, no CopilotKit wiring.

> This is the data foundation for Phase 2. When the AI issues (SAN-801–810) are activated after CopilotKit v2 migration, they call these tools rather than writing new queries. Consistency is the goal.

---

## Tool 1: `get_partner_profile`

```ts
// src/mastra/agents/partner/tools/get-partner-profile.ts
export const getPartnerProfile = createTool({
  id: "get_partner_profile",
  description: "Fetch full partner profile including services, locations, and asset counts",
  inputSchema: z.object({ partner_id: z.string().uuid() }),
  outputSchema: z.object({
    partner: PartnerOrganizationSchema,
    services: z.array(PartnerServiceSchema),
    location: PartnerLocationSchema.nullable(),
    photo_count: z.number(),
    completion_pct: z.number(),
  }),
  execute: async ({ partner_id }) => {
    // Supabase queries — runs server-side, identity pre-verified by API route
    const [partner, services, location, assetCount] = await Promise.all([
      supabase.from("partner_organizations").select("*").eq("id", partner_id).single(),
      supabase.from("partner_services").select("*").eq("partner_id", partner_id).eq("is_active", true),
      supabase.from("partner_locations").select("*").eq("partner_id", partner_id).maybeSingle(),
      supabase.from("partner_assets").select("id", { count: "exact" }).eq("partner_id", partner_id).eq("type", "photo"),
    ]);
    return { partner: partner.data, services: services.data ?? [], location: location.data, photo_count: assetCount.count ?? 0, completion_pct: partner.data?.profile_completion_pct ?? 0 };
  },
});
```

---

## Tool 2: `get_pending_leads`

```ts
export const getPendingLeads = createTool({
  id: "get_pending_leads",
  inputSchema: z.object({ partner_id: z.string().uuid(), limit: z.number().default(10) }),
  outputSchema: z.object({ leads: z.array(PartnerLeadSchema), total: z.number() }),
  execute: async ({ partner_id, limit }) => {
    const result = await supabase
      .from("partner_leads")
      .select("*", { count: "exact" })
      .eq("partner_id", partner_id)
      .in("status", ["new", "read"])
      .order("created_at", { ascending: false })
      .limit(limit);
    return { leads: result.data ?? [], total: result.count ?? 0 };
  },
});
```

---

## Tool 3: `get_revenue_summary`

```ts
export const getRevenueSummary = createTool({
  id: "get_revenue_summary",
  inputSchema: z.object({ partner_id: z.string().uuid(), window_days: z.number().default(30) }),
  outputSchema: z.object({
    current_total: z.number(),
    prior_total: z.number(),
    pct_change: z.number(),
    by_source: z.array(z.object({ source_type: z.string(), amount: z.number() })),
  }),
  execute: async ({ partner_id, window_days }) => {
    // Two queries: current window + prior window
    // Returns structured summary — no Gemini narrative (Phase 2 adds that in SAN-808)
  },
});
```

---

## Tool 4: `compute_health_score`

```ts
export const computeHealthScore = createTool({
  id: "compute_health_score",
  inputSchema: z.object({ partner_id: z.string().uuid() }),
  outputSchema: z.object({
    score: z.number(),
    tier: z.enum(["Thriving", "Growing", "Needs work", "At risk"]),
    breakdown: z.record(z.string(), z.number()),
  }),
  execute: async ({ partner_id }) => {
    // Calls compute_health_score() Supabase RPC (defined in CRM-009)
    const result = await supabase.rpc("compute_health_score", { p_partner_id: partner_id });
    return result.data;
  },
});
```

---

## Tool 5: `get_booking_requests`

```ts
export const getBookingRequests = createTool({
  id: "get_booking_requests",
  inputSchema: z.object({ partner_id: z.string().uuid(), status: z.enum(["pending","approved","all"]).default("pending") }),
  outputSchema: z.object({ bookings: z.array(VenueBookingSchema), total: z.number() }),
  execute: async ({ partner_id, status }) => {
    const query = supabase.from("venue_bookings").select("*", { count: "exact" }).eq("partner_id", partner_id);
    if (status !== "all") query.eq("status", status);
    const result = await query.order("requested_date", { ascending: true }).limit(20);
    return { bookings: result.data ?? [], total: result.count ?? 0 };
  },
});
```

---

## File structure

```
src/mastra/agents/partner/
  tools/
    get-partner-profile.ts
    get-pending-leads.ts
    get-revenue-summary.ts
    compute-health-score.ts
    get-booking-requests.ts
    index.ts              ← re-exports all 5
  index.ts                ← partnerAgent definition (SAN-705 owns this)
```

These tools are imported by `partnerAgent` (SAN-705) and also called directly from API routes for the static dashboard (no agent needed for Phase 1 dashboard data).

---

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] All 5 tools defined with correct inputSchema / outputSchema / execute
- [ ] Each tool runs against real Supabase data (no mocks in execute)
- [ ] Server-side identity verified before any Supabase call (F13 carve-out pattern)
- [ ] No Gemini / `@ai-sdk/google` imports in any tool file
- [ ] No `@anthropic-ai/*` imports
- [ ] Vitest: each tool's output shape matches schema for mocked Supabase responses

## Blocked by

* CRM-001 (schema), CRM-009 (health score RPC)

## Related

* SAN-705 (AGT-PTR-01) — partnerAgent registers these tools
* SAN-801–810 — Phase 2 AI issues call these tools from agent context
